      "score": 10,
      "comments": 9,
      "author": "gavinmorrow",
      "published": "2026-09-16T22:55:11Z",
      "bullets": [
        "While gzip streams concatenate natively via RFC 1952, tar archives mandate two 512-byte zero-filled blocks as an end-of-archive marker.",
        "Standard tar extractors halt processing at the first zero-block delimiter, silently ignoring all subsequent concatenated archive data.",
        "Proper concatenation requires stripping the 1,024-byte null trailer from the preceding tar stream prior to recompressing."
      ]
